iCube / dolphin-ios git hooks
=============================

Enable (once per clone or worktree):

    git config core.hooksPath .githooks

The pre-commit hook runs hygiene checks on STAGED files only (fast):

  - Swift under Source/iOS/App/   -> swiftformat --lint + swiftlint
  - iCube ObjC/ObjC++/C/C++ under Source/iOS/ -> clang-format --dry-run -Werror
        (uses Dolphin's Source/.clang-format via auto-discovery; the upstream
         C++ core under Source/Core is intentionally NOT format-checked here)
  - Source/Core/**.{cpp,h}        -> /tmp/syncheck.py syntax check, ONLY if that
        dev tool and a build-iphoneos-Release/compile_commands.json exist
        (normally absent -> silently skipped)

Modes (env vars):

    git commit                        # warn-only (default): prints findings, still commits
    ICUBE_HOOK_BLOCK=1 git commit     # block: lint *findings* abort the commit
    ICUBE_HOOK_SKIP=1  git commit     # skip all hygiene checks

Resilience:
  - A missing dev tool (swiftformat/swiftlint/clang-format/python3) is always a
    skip-with-warning, never a failure -- even in blocking mode. Blocking mode
    only blocks on real lint/format findings.
  - A missing .swiftlint.yml / .swiftformat is not fatal (tools fall back to
    defaults). Those configs are owned by the Swift side of the project.

Overrides:
    ICUBE_SYNCHECK=/path/to/syncheck.py   # point at a non-default syncheck
